1095		two-outcome POVMs that agree with the reported bit on answers of the form prescribed for a $\mathsf{Variable}$ question. The \emph{variable-measurement agreement distance} of $\mathcal S$ at $\mathsf{Variable}_j$ is
1096		\[
1097			\Delta_j(\mathcal S) = \sum_{b \in \F_2} \bigl\| \bigl( \hat A^{\mathsf{Variable}_j}_b \ot I_{\mathrm B} - I_{\mathrm A} \ot \hat B^{\mathsf{Variable}_j}_b \bigr) \ket{\psi} \bigr\|^2 \;,
1098		\]
1099		the squared state-dependent distance of Definition~\ref{def:povm-distance} between the two players' binary $\mathsf{Variable}_j$ effects on $\ket{\psi}$, under the one-point distribution and with the constant inside the $O(\cdot)$ taken to be $1$. It is not the consistency defect of Definition~\ref{def:consistency}, which is an off-diagonal outcome weight.
1100	\end{definition}
